Now we know that the vulnerability of all 151 vulnerable functions in our empirical study could not be decided without considering additional context, but what about secure functions? What proportion of functions labeled as secure—because they are not known to cause a vulnerability in the program—could potentially cause a vulnerability if an appropriate external context existed?

